	title 'PopUpDefProc'************************************************************************ PopUp Control Def Proc*** Copyright Apple Computer, Inc. 1988-92* All Rights Reserved** 26 Oct 88	Harry Yee** Finished initial coding for pop-ups** 18 Nov 88	Harry Yee** Finished resource support for pop-ups.** 21 Nov 88	Harry Yee** Changed do_track so that the x register upon exit, contains the part code* if mouse was in pop-up when released, if mouse was outside menu then x* contains zero. This needed to be changed because we were always getting a hit* even though the user would drag the mouse outside the pop-up and then release.* TRACKCONTROL also being changed to take advantage of this.** 23 Nov 88	Harry Yee** The control manager call MoveControl changed the pop-up control's main ctlRect,* but since the pop-up box's rect was stored internally it needed to be changed also.* I now change the moveCtl routine from a do nothing routine to change the pop-up box's* rect.** I now check the control's invisible bit before drawing the control.** FRightJustifyResult is now implemented. Changed routine DrawPopUp to make it work.** Bit 5 of the control's flag is now defined. If set the pop-up title will not be highlighted* when the pop-up is selected.** 01 Dec 88	Harry Yee** The pop-up's title is now also part of the pop-up control's "hot spot".** Pop-ups now work for an invalid initial value (BRC #38521, #38520)** In do_init I now check the pcount, if it is 9 then use default color table (which I now* define, I use to get this from the current menu bar's control record and I use do get in* the do_draw routine), if the pcount is 10 then then I use the ptr to the colorTable passed* by the app.** 12 Dec 88	Harry Yee** Fix problem with drawing pop-ups in color.** 15 Dec 88	Harry Yee** Bit 6 of the control's flag is now defined. If set the pop-up, when selected will be* drawn with white space if the whole pop-up cannot fit in the port and there is* room to add the white space to the pop-up.** Added do_key routine (#13) for handling command key equivalents in pop-ups.** 04 Jan 89 	Harry Yee** Fixed minor problem in do_test. The rectangle we were checking is a bit too large* because it was fudged in do_init to make things work correctly in the menu manager call* HiliteMenu. It was unfudged before making the check.** 30 Jan 89	Harry Yee** Whenever a NewValue defproc message got sent I would just call do_draw. This caused problems* because the ctlParam input was different for each call. I now have a separate defproc to handle* the NewValue message.** When the pop-up's title got hilited I hilited too much in 640 mode and not enough in 320 mode.* The above problem also arose when switching from one mode to another. _HiliteMenu has* been changed to fix this problem. BRC #40712.** 07 Feb 89	Harry Yee** In do_init if there is no color table specified then zero is stored in the ctlColor field* to specify that the default color table should be used. The GetColor routine in the* menu manager has been changed to special case for ctlColor being zero. This change was necesary* because when the menu manager was actually loaded into RAM i.e. old ROM, 4.1 system disk,* a SetBarColors would really fuck up the pop-up control's default color table.** 15 Mar 89	Harry Yee** Did away with DrawPopUp call so lots of things changed. This makes the pop-up* code much easier to maintain (now we don't have to go through menu manager, except* for drawing the title)** Fixed several bugs:*  ForeGround color was being changed but never restored. BRC #45534.*  If title was apple logo, title width was not getting set right. BRC #45146*  If there was no selection in the pop-up rect the ctlValue did not reflect*  this. If there is no selection, GetCtlValue will return zero. BRC #45143.** 16 Mar 89 	Harry Yee** Changed new_value routine. Didn't need to actually store the new control value* myself because the control manager already does this for us.** 23 Mar 89	Harry Yee** Fixed problem with ctlValue of zero. When ctlValue was zero, which means there* is no currently selected item in the pop-up, the first item in the pop-up menu* would always get drawn anyways. This was because a zero item ID to GetMItem* was not an invalid item ID but meant get the first item in the menu. So now I* check for ctlValue of zero before calling GetMItem. Worksheet #BCOJHS083.** When a pop-up is created, the height of the control rect is increased by one* to account for the bottom drop shadow. The bottom drop shadow needs to be* made a part of the control rect, so that it will erase correctly.** Now pop-ups are dimmed correctly when they are de-activated.** 27 Mar 89	Harry Yee** I now restore the text mode, foreground color, and text face after drawing result.** 29 Mar 89	Harry Yee** Add some additional control messages in my table. Only new one added that I do* anything about is the message sent when the state of the window that the pop-up* is in has changed. In this case I just invalidate the rect.** 30 Mar 89	Harry Yee** I now handle pcount=8 (which means InitialValue=0)** Color tables for pop-ups will now work with refs to handle and resources.** 07 Apr 89	Harry Yee** Fix do_test so that all I do is return my part code. Before I used to* check to make sure the pt passed was inside the pop-up rect (control mgr* already does the check for me). WorkSheet #BCORMR583.** 09 Apr 90	Harry Yee** Put back change made 07 Apr 89 since that wasn't it.** In do_track routine I was saving the PopUpMenuSelect return value in <currentSelection* which is defined on my stack. Routine DrawResult was using this same value to store* the master SCB which is why in 640 mode we always get the result that an item was* selected and in 320 mode nothing was ever selected. I now save <currentSelection on* the stack before calling DrawResult. WorkSheet #BCORMR583.** 12 Apr 89	Steven Glass** Reject events if control is invisible or inactive.** 27 Apr 89	Harry Yee & mensch & Johnny Joystick** Popup menus were not checking the ctrlparam field for zero in the drag routine. This caused* popups not to be able to be dragged with dragControl call.** 20 May 89	Yee** Was not disposing of the handle for the menu record when a pop-up control was being killed.** If the color table was a resource, it was not getting released. If it is a resource,* it now gets released in do_dispose.** 17-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** Changed rCtlColorTable to rCtlColorTbl.** 26-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** Now uses Get640Colors instead of having our own copy of color_patt (512 bytes).** 27-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** "If 0"-ed out experimental stuff from Harry that was trying to draw icons* in the pop-up result (and recalculate the control rect correspondingly).** 21-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Adding ctlMoreFlags bit 7, fDrawArrowIcon, to draw a down-arrow icon after* a pop-up menu's currently-selected item.** Adjusted the X coordinate to PopUpMenuSelect to make it line up right.** 9-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Added check to make the popped-up menu be at least as wide as the non-popped-up* representation.  This is especially cool if there's a down-arrow icon on the* right, because it looks really stupid to have that hanging out to the side while* the menu is popped up.** 15-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Added a missing call to derefMenuHand--the pop-up width stuff added above was* working sometimes, but not all the time.** 2-Jul-91	Dave Lyons** Changed GetOSIcon to GetSysIcon, removed macro.** 7-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** Added and then commented out code to disallow a pop-up to be set to*   a dimmed menu item.* Now releases rIcon resources to purge level 3 instead of -1.* SetCtlValue on a pop-up now draws the new value dimmed if the*   control is currently dimmed.************************************************************************* 13-Mar-92	Dave Lyons for 6.1** Use DrawStringWidth to draw the un-popped menu selection.* Minor optimizations (PEIs, ASL/LSR).** 16-Mar-92	Dave Lyons** Finished the DrawStringWidth mod in DrawResult (center truncate).* More optimizations.** 17-Nov-92	Dave Lyons** When handling a do_event message, only send keyDown and autoKey events* to MenuKey.  Preserve the menu bar around the MenuKey call, so we don't* accidentally leave the menu bar set to the pop-up menu control.***********************************************************************	blanks off	string asis	print push	print off	include 'all.macros'	include 'e16.event'	INCLUDE 'e16.control'	INCLUDE 'e16.quickdraw'	INCLUDE 'e16.menu'	INCLUDE 'e16.window'	INCLUDE 'e16.resources'oqdiconHeight 	EQU 4oqdiconWidth 	EQU 6;;;owmTaskData 	EQU 16	MACRO&lab	_GetResMTitle&lab	ldx #$440F	jsl $E10000	MENDTrue	equ $FFFFFalse	equ $0000	print pop	ENTRY MoveRect	ENTRY MoveRectIn	ENTRY PushPtrToRect	ENTRY PushPtrToRect2	ENTRY DerefMenuHand	ENTRY SetNewMenuBar	ENTRY SetupColorTable	ENTRY DrawPopUpBox	ENTRY DefColorTable	ENTRY Dimmed	ENTRY Nor_Mask	ENTRY DrawResult	ENTRY ClearResult***	ENTRY ReCalcPopUpRect	;incomplete from Harry (27-Sep-90 DAL);=======================================================================;; Some Global equates used throughout;MaxMessages	equ 19;; masks for control flag; (commented these out 17-Sep-90 DAL because they're in e16.menu now);;FType2PopUp	equ $0040	; 0 = normal popup, 1 = popup w/white space;FDontHiliteTitle	equ $0020	; 0 = hilite title, 1 = don't hilite title;FDontDrawTitle	equ $0010	; 0 = draw title, 1 = don't draw title;FDontDrawResult	equ $0008	; 0 = selection in pop-up rect, 1 = no selection drawn;FInWindowOnly	equ $0004	; 0 = use menumgr port, 1 = use current port;FRightJustifyTitle	equ $0002	; 0 = left justify title, 1 = right justify title;FRightJustifyResult equ $0001	; 0 = left justify result, 1 = right justify result;;FDrawResultOnly	equ $8000	; 0 = draw whole pop-up, 1 = draw result only;FPopUpInactive	equ $4000	; 0 = pop-up active, 1 = inactive;; masks for control moreflags;;MenuRefIsHandle	equ $0001	; menu ref is a handle;MenuRefIsResource	equ $0002	; menu ref is a resource ID;FMenuDefIsText	equ $0004	; menu ref is ptr to item list;fDrawIconInResult	equ $0020	; 0 = don't draw icon in result field, 1 = draw icon in resultfJustifyPopup	equ $0040	; 0 = no need for justification, 1 = Justify popup controlfDrawArrowIcon	equ $0080	; 1 = draw down-arrow icon after item (21-Jan-91 DAL)y1	equ 0	; rect offsetsx1	equ 2y2	equ 4x2	equ 6T_LEADING	equ 2	; Top leading.B_LEADING	equ 2	; Bottom leading._M_CACHE	equ $FFF7M_POPUP	equ $0001	; 0 = regular menu, 1 = pop-up menuNewCtlRecord	RECORD  0;---------------------------------------------------------------ctlNext	ds.l  1ctlOwner	ds.l  1ctlRect	ds.w  4ctlFlag	ds.b  1ctlHilite	ds.b  1ctlValue	ds.w  1ctlProc	ds.l  1ctlAction	ds.l  1ctlData	ds.l  1ctlRefCon	ds.l  1ctlColor	ds.l  1ctlReserved	ds.b  16ctlID	ds.l  1ctlMoreFlags	ds.w  1ctlVersion	ds.w  1ctlOptionalDataRecordSize;---------------------------------------------------------------; Values kept in ctlReserved by various controls;---------------------------------------------------------------;; Button Controls;ctlKey1	equ ctlReservedctlKey2	equ ctlKey1+1ctlKeyMods	equ ctlKey2+1ctlKeyModsCareBits	equ ctlKeyMods+2;; StatText Controls;ctlJust	equ ctlReserved	ENDR;=======================================================================;; This is the control record for a popup control;PopUpCtlRecord	RECORD  0ctlNext	DS.L  1ctlOwner	DS.L  1	; port containing the pop-up controlctlRect	DS.W  4	; total rectangle, title + pop-up boxctlFlag	DS.B  1ctlHilite	DS.B  1ctlValue	DS.W  1	; current selection for pop-upctlProc	DS.L  1	; control typectlAction	DS.L  1ctlData	DS.L  1ctlRefCon	DS.L  1ctlColor	DS.L  1	; ptr to color tableMenuRef	DS.L  1	; make this record look like a menu recordMenuEnd	DS.L  1	; signifies end of menu list, must be zeroPopUpRect	DS.W  4	; "hot spot" for popping up pop-upctlID	DS.L  1ctlMoreFlags	DS.W  1ctlVersion	DS.W  1TitleWidth	DS.W  1	; width of titleSize	DS.B  1	ENDR;=======================================================================;; This is the template record for a pop-up controlPopUpTemplate	RECORD  0pCount	DS.W  1	; parameter count (must be at least 6)ID	DS.L  1	; ID for the controlRect	DS.W  4	; bounding rectangleProcRef	DS.L  1	; Ref to DefProc, determines control typeFlags	DS.W  1	; old style flag wordMoreFlags	DS.W  1	; new flag wordRefCon	DS.L  1	; application definedTitleWidth	DS.W  1	; width reserved for pop up titleMenuRef	DS.L  1	; reference to menu record.InitialValue	DS.W  1	; initial value of the selected item in pop-upColorTableRef	DS.L  1	; if pCount = 10 then the colorTableRef is value is valid	ENDR;=======================================================================;; Define stack and direct page use	DEFINESTACKTemp	LONG	; define some local variablesCtlPtr	LONGRect	block 8Word1	wordWord2	wordWord3	wordWord4	wordWord5	wordWord6	wordWord7	wordOrigD	WORD	; caller's saved direct page registerOrigB	byte	; caller's saved data bank registerRtnAddr	block 3	; RTL address back to Control ManagertheCtlHandle	LONG	; handle to control recordCtlParam	LONG	; add'l parameter passed to DefProcCtlCode	WORD	; operation to performReturnValue	LONG	; space for return value to Ctl Mgr.ZPageSize	equ OrigD-Temp	title 'PopUpDefProc -- MainEntry'*****************************************************************PopUpProc	PROC EXPORT** This is the def_proc for PopUp controls.  When this* routine gets control, the stack looks as described below.**** Inputs:	On entry, the parameters are passed to us on the stack.**	|	| Previous Contents*	|-------------------|*	|    ReturnValue	| LONG - Space for return value*	|-------------------|*	|    CtlCode	| WORD - operation to perform*	|-------------------|*	|    CtlParam	| LONG - add'l parameter*	|-------------------|*	|    theCtlHandle	| LONG - Handle to control record*	|-------------------|*	|    RtnAddr	| 3 BYTES - RTL address*	|-------------------|*	|	| <-- Stack pointer** Outputs:	Put something into ReturnValue, pull off the parameters,*	and return to the Control Manager.**	|	| Previous Contents*	|-------------------|*	|    ReturnValue	| LONG - Space for return value*	|-------------------|*	|    RtnAddr	| 3 BYTES - RTL address*	|-------------------|*	|	| <-- Stack pointer** External Refs:	import do_draw	import do_nothing	import do_disposePopUp	import do_test	import do_init	import do_newvalue	import do_track	import do_move	import do_recsize	import do_key	import do_stateChange	import SelfMod1Low	import SelfMod1High	import SelfMod2Low	import SelfMod2High	import SelfMod3Low	import SelfMod3High** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	phb	; save the Data Bank register	phd	; save the Direct Page register	phk	; switch data bank to program bank	plb*** added 26-Sep-90 DAL (self-mod references to color_patt once)@flag	lda #0	bne @done	inc @flag+1	pha	pha	_Get640Colors	pla	sta SelfMod1Low+1	sta SelfMod2Low+1	sta SelfMod3Low+1	pla	sta SelfMod1High+1	sta SelfMod2High+1	sta SelfMod3High+1@done*** end of 26-Sep-90 addition	tsc	sec	sbc #ZPageSize	tcs	; switch Direct Page into stack	tcd	lda <CtlCode	cmp #recSize	beq SkipDeref	ldy #4	lda [<theCtlHandle],y	ora #$8000	; lock the handle	sta [<theCtlHandle],y	lda [<theCtlHandle]	; dereference the handle	sta <CtlPtr	ldy #2	lda [<theCtlHandle],y	sta <CtlPtr+2SkipDeref	lda <CtlCode	; get routine # to call	cmp #MaxMessages+1	blt ShiftIt	lda #6	; force unknown codes to null eventsShiftIt	asl a	tax	jsr (ActionTable,x)	sta <ReturnValue	; save the return value	stx <ReturnValue+2	lda <CtlCode	cmp #recsize	beq SkipUnlock	ldy #4	; unlock the control handle	lda [<theCtlHandle],y;	and #$7FFF	asl a	lsr a	sta [<theCtlHandle],ySkipUnlock	tsc	clc	adc #ZPageSize	tcs	lda <RtnAddr	; move the return address up	sta <ReturnValue-3	lda <RtnAddr+1	sta <ReturnValue-2	pld	; restore caller's Data Bank and	plb	; Direct Page registers	pla	; remove 10 bytes	pla	pla	pla	pla	lda #0	clc	rtl	; back to the caller;ActionTable	DC.W do_draw	0 Draw simple button.	DC.W do_nothing	1 Compute drag RECT.	DC.W do_test	2 Common hit test routine.	DC.W do_init	3 Initialize the control.	DC.W do_disposePopUp 4 Dispose.	DC.W do_draw	5 New value.	DC.W do_nothing	6 Compute Thumber constrains.	DC.W do_track	7 Drag the indicator.	DC.W do_nothing	8 Auto action.	DC.W do_newvalue	9 New value.	DC.W do_nothing	10 Set min max.	DC.W do_move	11 Move button.	DC.W do_recsize	12 Return size of standard record.	DC.W do_key	13 take key or menu event	DC.W do_nothing	14 ctlChangeTarget	DC.W do_nothing 	15 ctlChangeBounds	DC.W do_nothing	16 ctlWindChangeSize	DC.W do_nothing	17 ctlHandleTab	DC.W do_nothing	18 ctlHideCntl	DC.W do_StateChange	19 ctlWindStateChange, tells us state of control changed	ENDP	title 'PopUpDefProc -- do_recsize'*****************************************************************do_recsize	PROC** Returns the size of the control record.*** Inputs:*	none** Outputs:*	a-reg & x-reg hold result for def proc** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	lda #PopUpCtlRecord.Size	ldx #0		High word of size.	rts	ENDP	title 'PopUpDefProc -- Do_Nothing'*****************************************************************do_nothing	PROC** This is the routine we use when there is nothing to do.* It just returns zeros in the a and x registers.*** Inputs:*	ctlHandle*	ctlPtr** Outputs:*	a-reg & x-reg hold result for def proc** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	lda #0	Nothing flag.	tax	rts	ENDP	title 'PopUpDefProc -- Do_Init';=======================================================================;;	Do_Init;; Initialize a bunch of things and copy the pop-up template data into the; control record.;; Do_Init copies various fields from the PopUpTemplate to the Control Record.; The fields ID, Rect, ProcRef, Flags, MoreFlags and RefCon are automatically; copied from our template to the control record by the control manager.;; The main thing this routine does is calculate the pop-up's rect and the true; control rect depending on what the titlewidth is set.;;=======================================================================do_init	PROC	longa on	; mode	longi onfontheight	equ word1	; redefine some direct page locationsdescent	equ word2widmax	equ word3leading	equ word4title_width	equ word5	WITH PopUpCtlRecord	pha		; space for handle from one of the	pha		; newmenu calls	ldy #PopUpTemplate.MoreFlags	; first find out what format the	lda [<ctlparam],y		; menu is in, text stream or template	and #FMenuDefIsText		; call NewMenu for text stream,	bne CallNewMenu		; NewMenu2 for template	lda [<ctlparam],y	and #$0003		; menu is in format of MenuTemplate	pha		; get verb to find out whether menu is	ldy #PopUpTemplate.MenuRef+2	; a ptr, handle, or resource ID	lda [<ctlparam],y	pha		; reference to MenuTemplate	dey	dey	lda [<ctlparam],y	pha		; copies MenuTemplate, into a	_NewMenu2		; menu record returning handle to it	bra getmenuHandCallNewMenu	ldy #PopUpTemplate.MenuRef+2	; pointer to an array of menu lines and	lda [<ctlparam],y		; item lines	pha	dey	dey	lda [<ctlparam],y	pha		; let menu mgr parse our menu item list	_NewMenu		; create menu record and return handle to itgetmenuHand	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.MenuRef	pla	sta [<ctlPtr],y		; store the menu handle in our control	iny		; record	iny	pla	sta [<ctlPtr],y	ldy #MenuEnd	; must zero out the next four bytes after the location	lda #0	; where the menu ref is stored in the control record	sta [<ctlPtr],y	; remember, our control record has the same structure as	iny	; a menu bar record, so menuEnd signifies end of menu list	iny	sta [<ctlPtr],y;; calculate the width of the pop-up's title;	ldy #PopUpTemplate.Flags	lda [<ctlparam],y	tax	and #FDontDrawTitle	; first check if FDontDrawTitle flag is set, if it is then	beq @888	; title width is zero	lda #0	bra storeTitleWidth@888	ldy #PopUpTemplate.TitleWidth	lda [<ctlparam],y	; now check if app has specifically set a title width	beq @999	; if they have then use this width only if title left just.	tay	; save title width app has set	txa	; remember moreFlags still in x-reg	and #FRightJustifyTitle	bne @999	tya	bra storeTitleWidth@999	pha	; space for StringWidth call	pha	; space for ptr to menu title	pha	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.MenuRef+2	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<ctlPtr],y	; this routine checks to see if the menu title ref	pha	; is a ptr, handle, or resource ID  and	_GetResMTitle	; returns ptr (pascal string) to the menu title	lda 1,s	; check if the title is the apple logo	sta <temp	lda 3,s	sta <temp+2	lda [<temp]	cmp #$4001	beq ItsTheAppleLogo	cmp #$FF01	bne NotAppleLogoItsTheAppleLogo	pla	; get ptr to title off the stack	pla	lda #24	; width of apple logo	sta 1,s	bra GotWidthNotAppleLogo	_StringWidth	bra GotWidthstoreTitleWidth	phaGotWidth	jsr derefmenuhand	pla	ldy #oTitleWidth	sta [<temp],y	ldy #oMenuFlag	lda [<temp],y	and #_M_CACHE	; pop-up menus cannont be cached	ora #M_POPUP	; set the flag in menu that says menu is a pop-up	sta [<temp],y;==================================================;; Initialize some rects and calc a bunch of stuff;; first check to see if the user wants me to calculate the bottom right bounds of the; control rect for them	ldy #ctlRect	; move the current control record into our direct page	jsr MoveRect	; so we can get to it easier	lda <rect+y2	; is bottom of rect defined?	bne BottomDefined	pea 0 	; get current font size and calculate height of our pop-up	tdc	; space for font info record is on the stack	clc	adc #fontHeight	pha	_GetFontInfo	lda <descent	; get font height and add in some slop	clc	adc #B_LEADING	sta <descent	clc	adc <fontHeight	adc #T_LEADING	sta <fontHeight	adc <rect+y1	; we now have a new bottom	sta <rect+y2BottomDefined;------------------------------------------------------------; now we check the right side of the pop-up; right = length of title plus length of pop-up box;      length of title = actual length of title string or TitleWidth if non-zero;      length of pop-up = widest item in menu or whatever user as defined for right side	lda <rect+x2	; use apps right side?	bne RightDefined	jsr setNewMenuBar	; switch menu bars, orig menu bar is put on stack	jsr derefmenuhand	pea 0	; new width, 0 for automatic calculation	pea 0	; new heighth, 0 for automatic calculation***	ldy #oMenuID	; id of menu record (ZERO)	lda [<temp]	pha	_CalcMenuSize	; let the menu manager calculate widest item in the menu	jsr derefmenuhand	_SetMenuBar	; restore original menu Bar	jsr derefmenuhand	; deref menu handle one more time just in case it moved	ldy #PopUpTemplate.TitleWidth	lda [<ctlparam],y	; see if title width as been pre-defined	bne @777	; if it has use it, else get the titlewidth we		; calculated above	ldy #oTitleWidth	lda [<temp],y@777	ldy #oMenuWidth	; get width of widest item in menu	clc	adc [<temp],y	; add to width of pop-up's title to get right coordinate*** Added 21-Jan-91 DAL*** Allow 22 pixels of width for the down-arrow icon, if we're drawing one	pha	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlMoreFlags	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #fDrawArrowIcon	beq @noAdjust	pla	clc	adc #22	pha@noAdjust	pla*** end of 21-Jan-91 DAL	adc <rect+x1	sta <rect+x2RightDefined	inc <rect+y2	; we must account for the bottom drop shadow	ldy #PopUpRect	; now we define our popup rectangle, initially pop-up rect	jsr moveRectIn	; equals the rect of whole control	ldy #PopUpTemplate.TitleWidth	lda [<ctlparam],y	; check if app has pre-defined the title width	bne @666	; if it has use it, else get width we calc. above	ldy #oTitleWidth	lda [<temp],y@666	clc	adc <rect+x1	ldy #PopUpRect+x1	; now plug in the real left coordinate for the pop-up rect	sta [<ctlPtr],y	ldy #oTitleWidth	; just in case app wanted title right justified	sec	; we have to adjust left coord. of our control rect.	sbc [<temp],y	sta <rect+x1	ldy #ctlRect	jsr MoveRectIn	ldy #PopUpTemplate.pCount	lda [<ctlparam],y	cmp #8	beq NoInitialValue	ldy #PopUpTemplate.InitialValue	; get initial value of current selection	lda [<ctlparam],y		; for the pop-up and store in control rec	bra storevalueNoInitialValue	lda #0storevalue	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlValue	sta [<ctlPtr],y	ldy #PopUpTemplate.pCount	lda [<ctlparam],y	cmp #9	beq doDefault	ldy #PopUpTemplate.ColorTableRef	lda [<ctlparam],y	tax	iny	iny	lda [<ctlParam],y	bra storeItdoDefault	lda #0	; Zero for default color table	taxstoreIt	ldy #ctlColor+2	sta [<ctlPtr],y	; high word of color table	dey	dey	txa	; x contains low word of color table	sta [<ctlPtr],y	ENDWITH	lda #0	tax	rts	ENDP	title 'PopUpDefProc -- do_disposePopUp'*****************************************************************do_disposePopUp	PROC EXPORT** Test if the mouse is down in the control.*** Inputs:*	ctlParam = undefined*** Outputs:*	a-reg and x-reg are always zero** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.MenuRef+2	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	_DisposeHandle	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlmoreflags	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #$0010	; is the color table a resource	beq NotResource	PushWord #rCtlColorTbl	;was rCtlColorTable 17-Sep-90 DAL	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlColor+2	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	_CMReleaseResourceNotResource	lda #0	tax	rts	ENDP	title 'PopUpDefProc -- do_test'*****************************************************************do_test	PROC** Test if the mouse is down in the control.*** Inputs:*	ctlParam = point to check*** Outputs:*	a-reg and x-reg are always zero** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	pha	; space for result	pea 0000	; push pointer to point to check	tdc	clc	adc #ctlparam	pha	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.CtlRect	jsr MoveRect	; push ptr to the control rectangle	dec <rect+y2	; bottom drop shadow is not part of "hot spot"	jsr PushPtrToRect	_PtInRect	; is mouse in the pop-up control's rect	pla	beq Ignore	lda #$A0	bra GetOutIgnore	lda #0	Return that we want to ignore this.GetOut	ldx #0	high word zero	rts	ENDP	title 'PopUpDefProc -- Do_Draw'*****************************************************************do_draw	PROC** Draws the control using DrawPopUp.*** Inputs:*	ctlHandle*	ctlPtr*	ctlParam = high-order word tells us if control is active or not, $FFFF=not active*                              low-order word = part code.** Outputs:*	a-reg and x-reg are zero.** External Refs:	import LoadResource** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	WITH PopUpCtlRecordMode	equ word7	ldy #ctlFlag	; check if the invisible flag is set	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #$0080	; if high bit of flag is set then its invisible	beq notInvisible	brl noDrawnotInvisible	pha	; find out what mode we're in first	_GetMasterSCB	pla	and #$0080	sta <mode	jsr setNewMenuBar	; set menu bar to the control handle, old menu bar		; handle is still on the stack	jsr SetupColorTable	; set up color table and put in <word1	ldy #ctlflag	; first check if we need to draw a title	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #FDontDrawTitle	bne NoTitle	jsr derefmenuhand	; deref handle to menu and put in <temp	pea 0	; draw the pop-up's title	ldy #oMenuID	lda [<temp],y	pha	_HiliteMenuNoTitle	jsr DrawPopUpBox	; draw pop-up box and drop shadow	ldx #0	; flag for DrawResult that says PopUpBox was also drawn		; this flag tells us we don't have to do some extra setup		; work already done in DrawPopUpBox	jsr DrawResult	; draw current selection in pop-up box	lda <ctlParam+2	bpl active*** subrootinized 7-Dec-91 DAL	jsr DimMyRectangle***active	_SetMenuBar	; restore original system menu barnoDraw	lda #0	tax	rts*** subrootinized 7-Dec-91 DAL	export DimMyRectangleDimMyRectangle	pea dimmed>>16	pea dimmed	_SetPenMask	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.CtlRect+x1	lda [<ctlPtr],y	sta <rect+x1	jsr PushPtrToRect***	pea color_patt>>16	entry SelfMod1HighSelfMod1High	pea $7777	;26-Sep-90 DAL	lda [<word1]	and #$00F0	asl a***	adc #color_patt	entry SelfMod1LowSelfMod1Low	adc #$7777	;26-Sep-90 DAL	pha	_FillRect	pea nor_mask>>16	pea nor_mask	_SetPenMask	; restore pen mask	rts*** end of subrootinization, 7-Dec-91	ENDWITH	ENDP	title 'PopUpDefProc -- Do_NewValue'*****************************************************************do_newValue	PROC** Called by control manager in response to a _SetCtlValue call. This routine redraws the* result in the pop-up in response to a change in the selected item for the pop-up.*** Inputs:*	ctlHandle*	ctlPtr*	ctlParam = high-order word is previous value, low-order word is new value.** Outputs:*	a-reg and x-reg are zero.** External Refs:	import DimMyRectangle	;7-Dec-91 DAL** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	WITH PopUpCtlRecord	ldy #ctlFlag	; check if the invisible flag is set	lda [<ctlPtr],y	bit #$0080	; if high bit of flag is set then its invisible	bne doNothing	jsr SetNewMenuBar	jsr SetupColorTable	ldx #$FFFF	jsr DrawResult*** Skankified 7-Dec-91 DAL -- If control is dimmed, draw new value as dimmed, too.	phd	pha	pha	;space for GetWAP	pea 0	;system tool	pea $10	;control manager	_GetWAP	;get Control Manager direct page	tsc	tcd	ldy #$004E	;offset to Active flag	lda [1],y	;grab value from Control Manager workspace	plx	plx	pld	tax	bpl @noDim	jsr DimMyRectangle@noDim*** end 7-Dec-91	_SetMenuBardoNothing	rts	ENDP	title 'PopUp DefProc -- Do_Track'*****************************************************************do_track	PROC** This is the routine that is called when the mouse goes down* in the control.** The control manager calls this routine because, the* test routine returned a part code of $80.*** Inputs:*	none** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	WITH PopUpCtlRecordCurrentSelection	equ word7	lda <ctlParam	bne @notZero	lda #0	tax	rts@notZero	jsr setNewMenuBar	; set menu bar to that of the control, leaving original		; menubar still on the stack to be restored when we exit	pha	; get current port and leave on stack to be restored	pha	; later	_GetPort	ldy #ctlFlag	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #FDontDrawTitle	bne NoTitle	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #FDontHiliteTitle	bne NoTitle	jsr derefmenuhand	; dereference menu's handle and put pointer in <temp	PushWord #True	; hilite the control's title	ldy #oMenuID	lda [<temp],y	pha	_HiliteMenuNoTitle	ldy #PopUpRect	; convert the upper left corner of the rect to global	jsr MoveRect	jsr PushPtrToRect	_LocalToGlobal*** 9-Mar-91 DAL -- shift the rest of the rectangle to global coordinates	pea 0	tdc	adc #rect+4	pha	_LocalToGlobal*** end of 9-Mar-91 DAL	ldy #ctlFlag	; find out what port we should set to	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #FInWindowOnly	bne SamePort	pha	; use menu mgr's port so we can draw some long menus	pha	_GetMenuMgrPort	_SetPortSamePort	pha	; space for result	ldy #ctlValue	lda [<ctlPtr],y	; current selection	pha	lda <rect+x1	; upper left corner of where to draw current selection***	dec a	;added 21-Jan-91 DAL to make it line up perfectly	dec a***	pha	lda <rect+y1	pha	ldy #ctlFlag 	; popup flag, what type to draw (with or w/o white space)	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #FType2PopUp	pha*** 9-Mar-91 DAL: call CalcMenuSize again to allow for the arrow icon!	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlMoreFlags	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #fDrawArrowIcon	beq @noAdj	jsr derefMenuHand	;added 15-Mar-91 DAL	sec	;make the popped-up menu at least as wide as the control rect	lda <rect+x2	sbc <rect+x1	inc a	inc a	;make it a bit wider, for the shadow decoration on the right	tax	ldy #oMenuWidth	cmp [<temp],y	;current menu width	bcc @alreadyWide	phx	; new width	pea 0	; new heighth, 0 for automatic calculation***	ldy #oMenuID	; id of menu record (ZERO)	jsr derefmenuhand	; --> temp	lda [<temp]	pha	_CalcMenuSize@alreadyWide@noAdj*** end of 9-Mar-91 DAL	ldy #MenuRef+2	; handle to the menu record	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	_PopUpMenuSelect	; make call to PopUpMenuSelect	pla	sta <currentSelection	_SetPort	; restore original port	lda <currentSelection	beq NoSelection;;;This code works, but it's probably not a good feature.  Applications have no;;;other way to determine what item was selected, if they want to provide menu;;;item help for dimmed items in pop-up menu controls.;*** added 7-Dec-91 DAL -- don't allow a dimmed item to become the current value;	pha	;space for result;	pei <currentSelection;	_GetMItemFlag;	pla;	and #$0080;	bne NoSelection;	lda <currentSelection;*** end 7-Dec-91	ldy #ctlValue	sta [<ctlPtr],y	jsr SetupColorTable***	jsr ReCalcPopUpRect	   ;incomplete routine from Harry (27-Sep-90 DAL)	pei <currentSelection ; save it because DrawResult trashes this value	ldx #$FFFF	; flag for DrawResult to setup some additional things	jsr DrawResult	pla	sta <currentSelectionNoSelection	ldy #ctlFlag	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #FDontDrawTitle	bne bye	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #FDontHiliteTitle	bne bye	jsr derefmenuhand	; we need to keep derefing this guy because we can't lock		; down the handle because most menu mgr calls upon exit		; unlock this handle	PushWord #False	ldy #oMenuId	lda [<temp],y	pha	_HiliteMenubye	_SetMenuBar	ENDWITH	lda <currentSelection	beq noHit	ldx #$A0	; return part code for the pop-up	bra outnoHit	ldx #0out	lda #True	; tell control manage that we handled the drag.	rts	ENDP	title 'PopUp DefProc -- Do_Move'*****************************************************************do_Move	PROC Export** Updates the pop-up box's rect to the appropriate values. The ctlRect* has already been changed by the control manager.** Inputs:*	none** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.PopUpRect	jsr PushPtrToRect2	pei <ctlParam+2	pei <ctlParam	_OffSetRect	lda #0	tax	rts	ENDP	title 'PopUp DefProc -- Do_Key'*****************************************************************do_key	PROC Export** Handle a key or menu event.** The event.what will be an Event Manager event (typically* nullEvt, keyDownEvt, autoKeyEvt) or the special code* wInSpecial for a menu item (ID in taskData).** ctlParam is the event record.** Inputs:*	none** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on** 12 Apr 89	Steven Glass** Check the control record for inactive control and invisible* control.  If either is true, reject the event.*****************************************************************; Added 12 Apr 89 SEG	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlFlag	;Look at the flag and hilite bytes	lda [<ctlPtr],y	tax		;(save a momment)	and #$FF00		;If hilite is FF, we are inactive and should	cmp #$FF00		;ignore the event.	beq DontWantIt	txa		;Now, check the invis bit	and #$0080		;If invis, we don't want it either.	bne DontWantIt; End Addition*** added 17-Nov-92 DAL -- Only send keyDown and autoKey events to MenuKey	lda [<ctlParam]	cmp #keyDownEvt	beq @isKey	cmp #autoKeyEvt	bne DontWantIt@isKey*** Preserve menu bar around the MenuKey call	pha	pha	_GetMenuBar*** end 17-Nov-92 DAL	pei <ctlParam+2	;pointer to task record containing char to check	pei <ctlParam	pei <theCtlHandle+2	pei <theCtlHandle	_MenuKey*** added 17-Nov-92 DAL -- restore menu bar	_SetMenuBar*** end 17-Nov-92	ldy #owmTaskData	lda [<ctlParam],y	bne @1	brl DontWantIt@1	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlvalue	sta [<ctlPtr],y	jsr SetNewMenuBar	jsr SetupColorTable	ldx #$FFFF	jsr DrawResult	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlFlag	lda [<ctlPtr],y	; check if there is a title or not	and #FDontDrawTitle	bne noTitle	jsr derefmenuhand	pea 0	;unhilite the popup's title highlighted by MenuKey	ldy #oMenuID	lda [<temp],y	pha	_HiliteMenunoTitle	_SetMenuBar	lda #$FFFF	;Return true for having handled event	tax	rtsDontWantIt	lda #0	;Return False, don't want event.	tax	rts	ENDP	title 'PopUp DefProc -- Do_StateChange'*****************************************************************do_stateChange	PROC Export** This message is sent when the state of the window that the control is* in has changed.** Inputs:*	none** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlRect	jsr PushPtrToRect2	_InvalRect	tax	rts	ENDP*****************************************************************GetPopUpDefProc	PROC Export** Returns the address of the PopUp control def-proc.*** Inputs:*	space for pointer** Outputs:*	Pointer to DefProc** External Refs:	import PopUpProc** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	DefineStackRTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3ThePointer	LONG	lda #PopUpProc	sta ThePointer,s	lda #^PopUpProc	sta ThePointer+2,s	lda #0	clc	rtl	ENDP********************************************************************************** 	DerefMenuHand** Dereference the menu handle in PopUpCtlRecord.MenuRef and put ptr in our direct* page space Temp.*********************************************************************************derefMenuHand	PROC	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.MenuRef	lda [<ctlPtr],y	sta <temp	iny	iny	lda [<ctlPtr],y	sta <temp+2	lda [<temp]	tax	ldy #2	lda [<temp],y	sta <temp+2	stx <temp	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** 	SetupColorTable**	This routine puts the pointer to the pop-up control's* 	color table into our direct page space <word1. If the*	ctlColor field of the record is zero then we use the*	default color table defined in PopUpData.**  IN: <ctlPtr = ptr to pop-up's control record* OUT: <word1 = ptr to pop-up's color table (if ctlColor field is zero*               then we use the default color table)*********************************************************************************SetupColorTable	PROC	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlColor+2 ; get pop-up's color table	lda [<ctlPtr],y	; if this field is zero then it means we use	dey	; the default color table	dey	ora [<ctlPtr],y	beq @DefaultColor	; use default color table	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlColor	lda [<ctlPtr],y	sta <word1	iny	iny	lda [<ctlPtr],y	sta <word1+2	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlmoreflags	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #$0018	; bits 3 and 4 tell us what the color table is made of	beq @Done	bit #$0008	; Is color table a handle?	bne @ColorTableIsHandle@ColorTableIsResource	pha	pha	PushWord #rCtlColorTbl	;was rCtlColorTable 17-Sep-90 DAL	lda <word1+2	pha	lda <word1	pha	_CMLoadResource	pla	sta <word1	pla	sta <word1+2@ColorTableIsHandle	ldy #2	lda [<word1],y	tax	lda [<word1]	sta <word1	stx <word1+2	rts@DefaultColor	lda #DefColorTable	sta <word1	lda #^DefColorTable	sta <word1+2@Done	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** 	DrawResult**	This routine draws the currently selected menu item in*	the pop-up rect. It first checks whether the FDontDrawResult*	bit is set before doing anything. If the item ID in ctlValue*	is invalid (carry set coming back from GetMItem) then we clear*	whatever is currently in the pop-up rect and set ctlValue to zero.**  IN: <word1 : contains ptr to pop-up's color table (call SetupColorTable)*      pop-up control's record is the current menu bar (call SetNewMenuBar)*      x-reg : $0000 = don't need to setup popup rect in <RECT (already done by DrawPopupBox)*              $FFFF = we need to setup <RECT still*********************************************************************************DrawResult	PROC	import CheckForIconItemNameHdl	equ word3ItemNamePtr	equ word5mode	equ word7	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlFlag ; first check if result should be drawn	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #FDontDrawResult	beq okToDraw	brl outokToDraw	txa	; flag that tells us whether we're just drawing result	bpl SkipThisSetup	jsr ClearResultSkipThisSetup	pha	; space for result	pha	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlValue ; get pointer to currently selected item in pop-up menu	lda [<ctlPtr],y	beq @Invalid	; if ctlValue is zero, its means nothing currently selected	pha	; must special case zero because zero item id to GetMItem	_GetMItem	; means get first item in menu!!!	bcc @skipit	; item found@Invalid	pla	; clean up stack first	pla	brl Errout@skipit	pla	sta <itemNamePtr	pla	sta <itemNamePtr+2	stz <ItemNameHdl	stz <ItemNameHdl+2	pea 0	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlValue	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	_GetMItemFlag	pla	and #$C000	; mask off high two bits of item flag to get ref	beq pointer	; 00 = ptr	bpl handle	; 01 = handle	pha	; 10 = resource	pha	pea $8006	; string resource	pei <ItemNamePtr+2	pei <ItemNamePtr	_CMLoadResource	pla	sta <ItemNamePtr	pla	sta <ItemNamePtr+2handle	lda <ItemNamePtr	sta <ItemNameHdl	lda <ItemNamePtr+2	sta <ItemNameHdl+2	ldy #4	; first lock down handle	lda [<ItemNameHdl],y	ora #$8000	sta [<ItemNameHdl],y;;;	ldy #2	; deref the handle	dey	dey	lda [<ItemNameHdl],y	sta <ItemNamePtr+2	lda [<ItemNameHdl]	sta <ItemNamePtr	jsr SetupColorTable	; reset ptr to color table just in case memory moved		; from above load resourcepointer	jsr PushPtrToRect	; inset the rect to get it ready for drawing the result	pea 2	pea 1	_InsetRect	pha	; get foreground color and save on the stack	_GetForeColor	pha	_GetTextFace	; save original text face	pha	_GetTextMode	; save original text mode	pea 4	; Transfer foreground pixels only	_SetTextMode	pha	; clip title to the pop-up rectangle	pha	_GetClipHandle	pha	; get a new clip region	pha	_NewRgn	lda 3,s	pha	lda 3,s	pha	_SetClipHandle	jsr PushPtrToRect	_ClipRect	jsr PushPtrToRect	; put rect back the way it was before	pea $FFFE	pea $FFFF	_InsetRect	lda [<word1]	and #$000F	pha	asl a	asl a	asl a	asl a	ora 1,s	sta 1,s	xba	ora 1,s	sta 1,s	_SetForeColor	; set the color of the text	pha	; space for result	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlValue	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	_GetMItemStyle	_SetTextFace	pha 	; leading	pha 	; widmax	pha	; descent	pha	; ascent	tsc	inc a	pea 0	pha	_GetFontInfo	ply	; get ascent off stack	pla	; get descent off stack	ply	; get widmax off stack	ply	; get leading off stack	clc	adc #2	pha	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlFlag	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #FRightJustifyResult	beq LeftJustifyResult	pha	; space for result	pei <ItemNamePtr+2	pei <ItemNamePtr	_StringWidth	lda <Rect+x2	sec	sbc 1,s	sbc #3	bra storeLeftLeftJustifyResult	pha	; calculate amount of space to indent result	pea $57	_CharWidth	lda 1,s	ror a	clc	adc 1,s	adc <Rect+x1storeLeft	tax	pla	lda <Rect+y2	sec	sbc 1,s	ply	phx	pha	jsr CheckForIcon	; check to see if menu item has an icon associated with it		; and if we need to draw it.	lda 3,s	;X coord	sta >theXpos	_MoveTo;;	lda <ItemNamePtr+2;;	pha;;	lda <ItemNamePtr;;	pha;;	_DrawString*** 16-Mar-92 DAL -- use DrawStringWidth to draw result	pea $4000	;center-trunc, pstring ptr	pei <ItemNamePtr+2	pei <ItemNamePtr	;string pointer	sec	lda <Rect+x2	sbc >theXpos	pha	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlMoreFlags	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #fDrawArrowIcon	beq @drawResult	jsr GetNegIconWidth	adc 1,s	sta 1,s@drawResult	ldx #$1512	jsl $e10000;	_DrawStringWidth*** end 16-Mar-92*** Added 21-Jan-91 DAL*** If fDrawArrowIcon is set, draw a down-pointing arrow after the item	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlMoreFlags	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #fDrawArrowIcon	beq @noDownArrow	pha	pha	;space for GetSysIcon result	pea 2	;misc icons	pea 3	;down arrow icon	pha	pha	;long aux value (ignored)	_GetSysIcon	pea 0	;icon mode	jsr GetNegIconWidth	adc <Rect+x2	;right edge minus width or half-of-width	pha	lda <Rect+y1	inc a	;Ought to get the font height here	inc a	pha	_DrawIcon@noDownArrow*** end of 21-Jan-91 DAL	lda <ItemNameHdl+1	beq NoHandle	ldy #4	; unlock handle to the title	lda [<ItemNameHdl],y;	and #$7FFF	asl a	lsr a	sta [<ItemNameHdl],y	pea 0	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlValue	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	_GetMItemFlag	pla	bpl NotResource	; if zero then item string was not a resource	pea $8006	; pstring resource	pha	; result space for GetMItem	pha	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlValue	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	_GetMItem	_CMReleaseResourceNotResourceNoHandle	_DisposeRgn	_SetClipHandle	_SetTextMode	; restore original stuff	_SetTextFace	_SetForeColor	; restore original foreground colorout	rtsErrout	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlValue	lda #0	; zero ctlValue, this tells us there is no current selection	sta [<ctlPtr],y	rtstheXpos	dc.w 0** GetNegIconWidth*GetNegIconWidth	lda #22	jsr HalfIf320	eor #$ffff	sec	rts** HalfIf320 -- in 640 mode, return A unchanged, carry clear*              in 320 mode, return A cut in half, carry clear** (The carry is always clear so we can ADC when we come back)*HalfIf320	pha	pha	_GetMasterSCB	pla	and #$0080	bne @640	pla	lsr a	clc	rts@640	pla	clc	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** 	DrawPopUpBox**	Draws the pop-up rect and the drop shadow.**  IN: <word1 : contains ptr to color table for pop-up*      <word7 : contains flag to tell us what mode we're in*********************************************************************************DrawPopUpBox	PROCmode	equ word7	jsr ClearResult	; setup <RECT and fill background color of pop-up	ldx #1	; set the pen size	lda <mode	beq Not640	inxNot640	phx	; width of pen	pea 1	; height of pen	_SetPenSize***	pea color_patt>>16	; make sure pen pattern is setup according to	entry SelfMod2HighSelfMod2High	pea $7777	; 26-Sep-90 DAL	ldy #4	; pop-up menu's color table	lda [<word1],y	and #$00F0	asl a***	adc #color_patt	entry SelfMod2LowSelfMod2Low	adc #$7777	; 26-Sep-90 DAL	pha	_SetPenPat	jsr PushPtrToRect	; now frame it	_FrameRect;; --- Draw the drop shadow for the pop-up rect ---------------------------------------;	ldy <Rect+x2	; Pass last point	phy	lda <Rect+y1	clc	adc #4	pha	phy	; Pass second point	ldx <Rect+y2	phx	lda <Rect+x1	; Set starting point	clc	adc #5	pha	phx	_MoveTo	_LineTo	lda #1	ldx <mode	beq In320mode	inc aIn320mode	asl a	pha	pea 1	_SetPenSize	_LineTo	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** 	ClearResult**	This routine clears the item in the pop-up rect*	it also puts the popup rect in <RECT.**  IN: <ctlPtr : ptr to pop-up control record*      <word1 : contains ptr to pop-up control's color table* OUT: <RECT contains the pop-up rect (not including right drop shadow)*********************************************************************************ClearResult	PROC	pha	_GetMasterSCB	pla	and #$0080	sta <word7	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.PopUpRect	jsr MoveRect	ldy <Rect+x2	dey	dey	lda <word7	beq Its320	dey	deyIts320	sty <Rect+x2	dec <Rect+y2	; adjust for bottom drop shadow	jsr PushPtrToRect	ldx #1	lda <word7	beq pushit1	inxpushit1	phx	pea 1	_InsetRect	jsr PushPtrToRect	; no valid current selection***	pea color_patt>>16	entry SelfMod3HighSelfMod3High	pea $7777	; 26-Sep-90 DAL	lda [<word1]	and #$00F0	asl a***	adc #color_patt	entry SelfMod3LowSelfMod3Low	adc #$7777	; 26-Sep-90 DAL	pha	_FillRect	jsr PushPtrToRect	ldx #$FFFF	lda <word7	beq pushit2	dexpushit2	phx	pea $FFFF	_InsetRect	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** 	SetNewMenuBar** Saves the handle to the old menu bar on the stack and then sets the new menu bar* to that of the control handle.*********************************************************************************setNewMenuBar	PROC	pla	; get rts off the stack	sta <word1	pha	; save original menubar on the stack	pha	_GetMenuBar;	lda <theCtlHandle+2	; make the new menu bar the popup control;	pha;	lda <theCtlHandle;	pha*** opt 13-Mar-92 DAL	pei <theCtlHandle+2	; make the new menu bar the pop-up control	pei <theCtlHandle***	_SetMenuBar	lda <word1	pha	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** MoveRect** Moves the rectangle from the control record* to direct page.** The source rectangle is specified by placing* its offset in the y-reg.*********************************************************************************MoveRect	PROC	ldx #0	; copy rect to d page@1	lda [CtlPtr],y	sta rect,x	iny	iny	inx	inx	cpx #8	bcc @1	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** MoveRectIn** Moves the rectangle from direct page to the control record** The destination rectangle is specified by placing* its offset in the y-reg.*********************************************************************************MoveRectIn	PROC	ldx #0@1	lda Rect,x	sta [CtlPtr],y	iny	iny	inx	inx	cpx #8	bcc @1	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** PushPtrToRect** Pushes pointer to controls bounding rect.*********************************************************************************PushPtrToRect	PROC	ply	; save rts	pea 0000	tdc	clc	adc #Rect	; get address of rect on stack	pha	phy	; restore rts	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** PushPtrToRect2** Y contains the offset of the pointer to the rectangle to push on the stack.*********************************************************************************PushPtrToRect2	PROC	plx	; save return address	tya	; y contains the offset in control record of rect to push	clc	adc CtlPtr	; base address of control record	tay	lda CtlPtr+2	; high word of address	adc #0	pha	; push address on the stack	phy	phx	; restore the return address	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************PopUpData	PROC; --- Masks for dimmed and normal text -----------------------------	ENTRY dimmeddimmed	DC.B $55,$AA,$55,$AA,$55,$AA,$55,$AA	ENTRY nor_masknor_mask	DC.B $FF,$FF,$FF,$FF,$FF,$FF,$FF,$FF; --- Default menu bar color table ---------------------------;	ENTRY DefColorTableDefColorTable	DC.W $00F0	Normal color, black	text on white.	DC.W $000F	Hilited color, white text on black.	DC.W $0000	Outline color, black.	ENDP	if 0 then	;incomplete stuff from Harry (27-Sep-90 DAL)********************************************************************************** 	ReCalcPopUpRect** This routine recalculates the size of the popup rectangle based on the* currently selected item.**********************************************************************************ReCalcPopUpRect	PROCmode	equ word7	ldx <ctlPtr+2	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlFlag	lda [<ctlptr],y	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.PopUpRect	and #FJustifyPopup	beq @NoJustification	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlRect@NoJustification	tya	clc	adc <ctlPtr	bcc @noCarry	inx@noCarry	phx	pha	_EraseRect	pha	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlValue	lda [<ctlptr],y	pha	ldx #$4E0F		; call GetItemWidth	jsl $E10000	pla		; Recalculate new popup rectangle	clc		; and update the control record.	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.PopUpRect+x1	adc [<ctlptr],y	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.PopUpRect+x2	sta [<ctlptr],y	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlRect+x2	sta [<ctlptr],y		; update the control rect also	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlFlag	lda [<ctlptr],y	and #FJustifyPopup	beq NoJust	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlRect+x2	lda [<ctlPtr],y	sec	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlRect+x1	sbc [<ctlPtr],y	pha	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlData+2	lda [<ctlptr],y	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlData	sec	sbc [<ctlptr],y	sec	sbc 1,s	clc	ror a	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlData	clc	adc [<ctlptr],y	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlRect+x1	sta [<ctlptr],y	clc	adc 1,s	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlRect+x2	sta [<ctlptr],y	tax	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.PopUpRect+x2	lda [<ctlptr],y	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.PopUpRect+x1	sec	sbc [<ctlptr],y	sta 1,s	ldy #Popupctlrecord.popuprect+x2	txa	sta [<ctlptr],y	ldy #Popupctlrecord.popuprect+x1	sec	sbc 1,s	sta [<ctlptr],y	pla	jsr derefmenuhand	; deref handle to menu and put in <temp	pea 0	; draw the pop-up's title	ldy #oMenuID	lda [<temp],y	pha	_HiliteMenuNoJust	PushWord <word7		; Save contents of dpage var <word7;			; since routine DrawPopUpBox uses it.	jsr SetupColorTable	jsr DrawPopUpBox	pla		; restore <word7, whether or not its in use currently	sta <word7	rts	ENDP	endif		;27-Sep-90 DAL********************************************************************************** 	CheckForIcon** This routine checks to see if the currently selected item has an icon* associated with it and if it does do we need to draw it.*********************************************************************************CheckForIcon	PROC export	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlMoreFlags	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #FDrawIconInResult	beq Error	pha		; space for result	pha	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlValue	; get id of selected menu item	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	_GetMItemIcon	bcc GotIconNoIcon	plx	plxError	brl DontDrawIcon		; clean up stack and return errorGotIcon	lda 1,s	ora 3,s		; see if a valid icon ref was passed back	beq NoIcon	pha		; space for result	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlValue	; get id of selected menu item	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	_GetMItemFlag2	pla	and #$0003		; low 2 bits of ItemFlag2 tell us how icon is ref.	tax		; move how icon will be referenced in x-reg	pha		; space to store iconRef that might need to get released	pha	ldy #PopUpCtlRecord.ctlFlag	; get title justification information	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #$0001	pha;; ----- Setup new stack frame ----------------------------------------------------------------;	DefineStackDPage	equ 1Justification	equ DPage+2IconID	equ Justification+2TheIconRef	equ IconID+4theRTS	equ TheIconRef+4yCoord	equ theRTS+2		; position in local coords. that text is to drawnxCoord	equ yCoord+2	phd	tsc	tcd	txa		; y-reg defines how icon will referenced	asl a		; turn into index to table	tax	jmp (Table,x)Table	dc.W doPointer	dc.W doHandle	dc.W doResource	dc.W Error		; invalid value in moreflagsdoResource	lda <Justification		; set bit to indicate icon was a resource	ora #$8000	sta <Justification	lda <TheIconRef		; store id of icon resource so we can use it later	sta <IconID		; to dispose of this resource	lda <TheIconRef+2	sta <IconID+2	pha		; space for result	pha	PushWord #rIcon	PushLong <TheIconRef	_LoadResource	bcc LoadedOk	pld		; restore original direct page register	brl NoIconLoadedOk	pla		; put hdl to icon in a dpage variable	sta <TheIconRef	pla	sta <TheIconRef+2doHandle	ldy #2		; deref handle to icon	lda [<TheIconRef],y	tax	lda [<TheIconRef]	sta <TheIconRef	stx <TheIconRef+2doPointer;; ----- Get ready to make _DrawIcon call ------------------------------------------------------------;	PushLong <TheIconRef	; ptr to icon	pea 0		; display mode	PushWord <xCoord		; x coordinate	lda <DPage	tax	ldy #oQDIconWidth	lda [<TheIconRef],y	tay	lda >Word7,x	beq @In320	tya	asl a	tay@In320	lda <Justification	and #$0001	bne RightJust	tya	clc	adc <xCoord	adc #2	sta <xCoord	bra TitleCoordFudgedRightJust	tya	sta 1,s	lda <xCoord	sec	sbc 1,s	sbc #2	sta 1,sTitleCoordFudged	lda <DPage	tax	lda >Rect+y2,x	sec	sbc >Rect+y1,x	ldy #oQDIconHeight	sec	sbc [<TheIconRef],y	clc	ror a	pha	lda >Rect+y1,x	clc	adc 1,s	sta 1,s*** added 21-Jan-91 DAL for 640 dithering	lda 3,s;	and #$fffe	lsr a	asl a	sta 3,s*** end of 21-Jan-91 DAL	_DrawIcon		; draw the icon in the popup box	lda <Justification		; check flag to see if icon was resource	bpl NotResource		; if it was then we need to release the resource;;;	PushWord #$FFFF		; neg. purge level which means handle gets disposed	pea 3		;purge level 3 (7-Dec-91 DAL)	PushWord #rIcon	PushLong <IconID	_ReleaseResourceNotResource	pld		; restore direct page	tsc		; clean up stack	clc	adc #10	tcsDontDrawIcon	rts	ENDP	END